course: dictionary
lesson: 473
title: Arrive and arrival
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To arrive means to get to a place at the end of a trip. «It is 2:35 and they arrive at 3:10.» The clue is the time: the trip ends when they get there, not when they leave.
explain: Arrive can also mean to come or to happen. «Spring has arrived» does not mean anyone reached a place. It means spring has come. In «rain that fell far away takes months to arrive», the rain is moving slowly, and it reaches the river at the end of a long journey.
explain: Small words after arrive matter. Use arrive at for a place or an answer, and arrive in for a city or country. Check your meaning by swapping in get to or reach. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: To arrive means to get to a place at the end of a trip.
fact: «Spring has arrived» means spring has come.
fact: Use arrive at for a place or an answer, and arrive in for a city or country.
fact: «Arrival» is the noun, the moment when someone or something gets somewhere.
fact: To arrive on time means to get somewhere at the time you were expected.
exercise: «It is 2:35 and they arrive at 3:10.» What time do they arrive? | 3:35 | *3:10 | 2:10 | 2:35
exercise: «Rain that fell far away takes months to arrive.» What does arrive mean here? | To sing loudly | To dry up | *To reach the river after a long journey | To fall down again
exercise: Choose the right word: We will ____ Edinburgh at noon. | at | by | on | *in
test: «Spring has arrived.» What does arrived mean here? | *Has come | Has run away | Has left | Has been painted
test: Yuki thinks hard and arrives at the answer. What does arrives at mean? | Guesses at random without looking | *Reaches the answer after thinking | Writes the answer in pen | Loses the answer
exam: Which phrase is correct for a train reaching London? | arrive by London | arrive on London | arrive at London | *arrive in London
